{
 "about": "M1-82: where each playable exterior stands on the real LOLA terrain (M1-34) when the campaign gives it ground from the terrain provider (Atik's TerrainStream, M1-36). Authored per room: region_id, origin_xz_m, ephemeris_site, horizon_site, omit_staging_floor and the reason. Everything else is derived from the region's detail heightfield by game/tools/test_exterior_terrain.gd -- --write and checked on every test run. The flat greybox rooms are unchanged when the terrain is not used.",
 "frame": "Room-local = region site frame - origin_m, same axes (X toward 90 deg E on the map, Z = -map y, Y up), no rotation. Put the TerrainStream node at position -origin_m beside the room (room at the campaign origin), configure(region_id, origin_m + local point, exclusions) and move_focus(player.position + origin_m). exclusions are in the site frame; every other position is room-local.",
 "rules": "Anchors and focus targets keep their flat XZ and stand on the ground there (a focus target keeps its height above the floor). Props, fixtures and doors rest at the lowest ground under the part that meets the ground (vertices within 0.15 m of the base), so nothing floats; bury_m is the deepest corner, at most 0.6 m or 10 % of footprint_m (a graded pad). focus_approaches are 1.5 m from each target toward the player anchor, turned in 15 deg steps until the straight lane clears every door and prop collider; a lane that still cannot go straight goes through the one waypoint in detours (keyed by focus target or anchor id). Exclusions (site frame, TerrainStream clear areas) keep rock scatter off every anchor, approach, target, prop, fixture and door and off 2 m-spaced lanes from the player anchor to each of them. Walkable: at most 15 deg (the VIPER design incline the relay road already uses) along every lane (max_walk_slope_deg). ground_y_range_m is the room-local ground over the whole room footprint.",
